  "description": "Turn a request into an object you can queue, log, run later or undo: undo/redo stacks, macros, and the kernel's work_struct.",
  "hero": {
    "tag": "header",
    "attrs": {
      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span>\n    <span class=\"time\">45 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Behavioral pattern</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Tier 2: know intent, structure, one example</span>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Command</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Turn \"do this\" into an object you can hold in your hand: store it, queue it, log it, send it to another thread, or undo it. You already know this pattern as <code>struct work_struct</code>; here you learn the interview vocabulary, undo/redo with two stacks, and macros.</p>\n  <p class=\"small prereq\"><b>Before this page:</b> <a href=\"{{BASE}}lld/lld-oop-interfaces\">Interfaces</a> (program to an interface), <a href=\"{{BASE}}lld/lld-oop-polymorphism\">Polymorphism</a> (one call, many bodies), and <a href=\"{{BASE}}lld/lld-uml-class\">UML class diagrams</a> for the notation in the Structure picture (arrows and diamonds: <a href=\"{{BASE}}lld/lld-uml-relationships\">relationships</a>).</p>\n"
  },
